module ned-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6 }

// The District of Nebraska's own periods, computed under the federal rules
// (NECivR 6.1(a): FRCP 6 applies to any period these rules state). Rules
// that state no period or limit stay out: filing fees and in forma
// pauperis applications (NECivR 3.2, 3.3), summonses (4.1), electronic
// filing, service, privacy and discovery filing (5.1-5.4), proposed
// orders, stipulations, certified questions and sealing (7.2-7.5),
// pleading special matters (9.1), form of documents (10.1), amended
// pleadings (15.1), scheduling orders and the final pretrial conference
// (16.1(a)-(b), 16.2), class actions (23.1), disclosure, discovery
// stipulations and the interrogatory, production and admission formats
// (26.1-36.1), jury demand notation (38.1), argument (39.1), jury
// selection and deliberation (47.1-48.2), fee applications (54.3, 54.4),
// default (55.1), satisfaction of judgment (58.1), sureties and deposits
// (65.1-67.1), magistrate judges' duties and consent (72.1, 72.3, 73.1)
// and removed motions (81.1). Periods stated in units lit/core does not
// count stay in notes: written objections to an edited video served at
// least 24 hours before it is shown (NECivR 32.1(c)) and notice of a
// settlement at least 24 hours before trial to avoid juror costs (54.2).
// The court's own periods are not declared: the pro se progression order
// issues "approximately 30 days" after the last answer (16.1(c)). Other
// periods stay in notes because the rule does not say what they run
// from or binds the court, not a party: a response to a motion to exceed
// the word limits "within 7 days" (7.1(d)(1)(F)), the exhibit list
// delivered "on the day before the trial begins" (39.3(a)), a file
// checked out of the clerk's office returned "no later than 7 days"
// (79.1(d)) and exhibits retained at least 1 year after the judgment is
// final (79.1(f)(1)(A)(i)). The jury has 6 to 12 members (48.1). The
// earlier D. Neb. outline's FRCP flow and its decisions (Twombly, Iqbal,
// Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby; Johnson v. Dayton Elec. Mfg. Co.,
// Braden v. Wal-Mart Stores and Torgerson v. City of Rochester in the
// Eighth Circuit) are FRCP authority and belong to lit/frcp; they are
// removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A supporting or opposing brief: at most 13,000 words except with the
/// court's prior permission; all text, including the caption, headings,
/// footnotes and quotations, counts, and the brief carries a certificate
/// of the word count (NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(A), (C), (D)). The limit applies to
/// summary judgment briefs but not to the statement of material facts or
/// the response to it (NECivR 56.1(a)(4)).
limit brief { words <= 13_000 cite "NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(A)" } cite "NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(A)"
/// A moving party's reply brief: at most 6,500 words except with the
/// court's prior permission (NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(B)).
limit reply-brief { words <= 6_500 cite "NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(B)" } cite "NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(B)"
/// A motion for permission to exceed the word limits, and a response in
/// opposition to it: each at most 500 words (NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(F)).
limit word-limit-motion { words <= 500 cite "NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(F)" } cite "NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(F)"

/// A motion to dismiss, for judgment on the pleadings, for a more definite
/// statement or for summary judgment, and its supporting brief, are filed
/// and served (NECivR 7.1(b)(1)(B)).
event DispositiveMotionServed() paper brief
/// Any other motion and its supporting brief are filed and served (NECivR
/// 7.1(b)(1)(B)).
event MotionServed() paper brief
/// The opposing party files and serves its brief opposing a motion for
/// summary judgment (NECivR 7.1(c)(1)).
event SummaryJudgmentOppositionServed() paper brief
/// The opposing party files and serves its brief opposing any other motion
/// (NECivR 7.1(c)(1)).
event OppositionServed() paper brief
/// A reply brief is filed (NECivR 7.1(c)).
event ReplyFiled() paper reply-brief
/// A motion for permission to exceed the word limits is filed and served
/// (NECivR 7.1(d)(1)(F)).
event WordLimitMotionFiled() paper word-limit-motion
/// A party receives the notice of electronic filing of a document whose
/// authenticity or electronic signature it disputes (NECivR 11.1(a)).
event NefReceived()
/// The court rules on a party's motion to dismiss (NECivR 12.1).
event MotionToDismissRuled()
/// Trial begins on the date scheduled (NECivR 30.1(f), 39.2(a), 51.1,
/// 52.1).
event TrialBegins()
/// The edited video deposition is shown at trial (NECivR 32.1(c)).
event VideoShown()
/// The notice of removal is served (NECivR 40.1(b)).
event RemovalNoticeServed()
/// A motion requesting a place of trial different from the one first
/// requested is filed (NECivR 40.1(b)).
event PlaceOfTrialMotionFiled()
/// The trial judge designates a place of trial different from the one
/// requested (NECivR 40.1(d)).
event PlaceOfTrialDesignated()
/// The attorneys notify the court or clerk that the parties have settled
/// (NECivR 41.1).
event SettlementNotified()
/// The court dismisses a settled action for failure to file the
/// terminating documents (NECivR 41.1).
event SettlementDismissalEntered()
/// The adverse party receives notice of a subpoena for production or
/// inspection to be served on a nonparty (NECivR 45.1(a)).
event SubpoenaNoticeReceived()
/// Judgment is entered (NECivR 54.1(b), 79.1(f)(1)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A verdict is rendered (NECivR 79.1(f)(1)).
event VerdictRendered()
/// The movant serves its summary judgment motion and supporting statement
/// of material facts (NECivR 56.1(b)(3)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() paper brief
/// The opposing party serves a statement of additional material facts
/// (NECivR 56.1(c)).
event AdditionalFactsServed()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's order or findings and
/// recommendations (NECivR 72.2(a)).
event MagistrateOrderServed()
/// A party is served with a statement of objections to a magistrate
/// judge's order or findings and recommendations (NECivR 72.2(a)).
event ObjectionsServed() paper brief

/// NECivR 7.1(b)(1)(B): a brief opposing a motion to dismiss, for judgment
/// on the pleadings, for a more definite statement or for summary judgment
/// is filed and served within 21 days after the motion and supporting
/// brief are filed and served. Failure to file it is not a confession of
/// the motion but precludes contesting the movant's statement of facts
/// (NECivR 7.1(b)(1)(C)).
deadline dispositive-opposition-period: 21.days after DispositiveMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 7.1(b)(1)(B)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 7.1(b)(1)(B): a brief opposing any other motion is filed and
/// served within 14 days after the motion and supporting brief are filed
/// and served.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 7.1(b)(1)(B)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 7.1(c)(1): a reply brief and index of evidence supporting a
/// motion for summary judgment may be filed within 14 days after the
/// opposing party files and serves the opposing brief. Further briefs need
/// leave (NECivR 7.1(c)(3)); the motion is submitted when the reply time
/// expires (NECivR 7.1(g)).
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentOppositionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 7.1(c)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 7.1(c)(1): a reply brief supporting any other motion is filed
/// and served within 7 days after the opposing party files and serves the
/// opposing brief.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after OppositionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 7.1(c)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 11.1(a)(1)(B), (2)(B), (3)(B): a party challenging the
/// authenticity of an electronically filed document or of a signature on
/// it files an objection within 7 days of receiving the NEF.
deadline signature-objection-period: 7.days after NefReceived() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 11.1(a)(1)(B)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 12.1: when a party files a motion to dismiss, its time to answer
/// all claims, including those the motion does not address, is suspended
/// until 14 days after the court rules on the motion.
deadline answer-after-ruling-period: 14.days after MotionToDismissRuled() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 12.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 30.1(f): the party seeking to use a video deposition at trial
/// submits unresolved objections in a motion in limine, with a transcript,
/// no later than 7 days before trial or, alternatively, the date the
/// pretrial order sets.
deadline video-objections-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 30.1(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 32.1(c): at least 7 days before showing the video, the party
/// seeking to use it delivers a copy of the edited video to opposing
/// attorneys; their written objections are served at least 24 hours
/// before it is shown.
deadline edited-video-period: 7.days before VideoShown() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 32.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 39.2(a): unless ordered otherwise, each party files a trial brief
/// at least 7 days before the trial begins.
deadline trial-brief-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 39.2(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 40.1(b): the plaintiff in a removed action may file a written
/// request for trial at Omaha, Lincoln or North Platte within 14 days
/// after service of the notice of removal.
deadline removed-place-of-trial-period: 14.days after RemovalNoticeServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 40.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 40.1(b): a request for a place of trial different from the one
/// first requested is filed as a motion, and any other party then has 14
/// days to respond.
deadline place-of-trial-response-period: 14.days after PlaceOfTrialMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 40.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 40.1(d): responses to the trial judge's designation of a
/// different place of trial are filed within 14 days of the designation
/// unless the trial judge specifies a shorter time.
deadline designation-response-period: 14.days after PlaceOfTrialDesignated() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 40.1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 41.1: within 30 days after notifying the court or clerk of a
/// settlement, the attorneys file all documents necessary to terminate the
/// action, unless the court directs otherwise by written order; otherwise
/// the court may dismiss without further notice and without prejudice.
deadline settlement-papers-period: 30.days after SettlementNotified() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 41.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 41.1: after such a dismissal, the case may be reinstated within
/// 30 days after the date of the order on a showing of good cause why the
/// parties did not consummate the settlement.
deadline reinstatement-period: 30.days after SettlementDismissalEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 41.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 45.1(b): after receipt of notice of a nonparty subpoena for
/// production or inspection, the adverse party has 7 days to serve written
/// objections on the noticing party; no contested subpoena issues until
/// the objections are resolved.
deadline subpoena-objection-period: 7.days after SubpoenaNoticeReceived() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 45.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 51.1(a): unless ordered otherwise, each party files requested
/// jury instructions 7 days before the first day of trial.
deadline jury-instructions-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 51.1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 51.1(b): objections to requested jury instructions, with
/// supporting authority, are filed at least 3 days before the first day of
/// trial.
deadline instruction-objections-period: 3.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 51.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 52.1: in a civil nonjury trial, parties should file their
/// proposed findings of fact at least 7 days before the first day of
/// trial.
deadline proposed-findings-period: 7.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 52.1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 54.1(b), (d): a party entitled to recover costs files a verified
/// bill of costs within 30 days after entry of judgment; post-trial
/// motions do not extend the time, and a party who does not file within
/// it waives taxable costs.
deadline bill-of-costs-period: 30.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 54.1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 56.1(b)(3): the opposing party's brief and response to the
/// movant's statement of material facts may be filed within 21 days after
/// service of the motion and supporting statement.
deadline summary-judgment-response-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 56.1(b)(3)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 56.1(c): when the opposing party submits a statement of
/// additional material facts, the movant serves and files its responses
/// within 14 days after service of the opposing statement.
deadline additional-facts-response-period: 14.days after AdditionalFactsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 56.1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 72.2(a): a party objects to a magistrate judge's order or
/// findings and recommendations within 14 days after being served with
/// them, unless the order or recommendation states a different time.
deadline magistrate-objections-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 72.2(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 72.2(a): unless ordered otherwise, an opposing party may file an
/// opposing brief within 14 days of being served with the statement of
/// objections; the objecting party may not reply without leave.
deadline magistrate-opposition-period: 14.days after ObjectionsServed() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 72.2(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 79.1(f)(1): within 14 days after a verdict is rendered, the
/// offering attorney withdraws all exhibits in the clerk's custody and
/// gives the clerk a receipt.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-verdict-period: 14.days after VerdictRendered() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 79.1(f)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// NECivR 79.1(f)(1): within 14 days after a judgment is entered, the
/// offering attorney withdraws all exhibits in the clerk's custody.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-judgment-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6 cite "NECivR 79.1(f)(1)"
{
  forum frcp
}
